    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Isaac Paredes** earns the top spot in our lineup with a 70.39 efficiency score, driven by a favorable matchup against Rodriguez, G and a prime spot in the #3 hole. The pairing of **Brice Turang** (61.75) and **Henry Bolte** (61.38) provides a high-upside anchor at the top of the order; both benefit from an excellent matchup against Dobnak, whose 4.70 xERA offers significant room for run production. **Max Muncy** also clears the 60.00 threshold, effectively neutralizing his platoon disadvantage against a right-handed pitcher through his superior situational placement and the high projected ceiling against the same Dobnak-led staff. \n\nThe decision-making process for the remaining slots remains heavily focused on our premium on stolen bases and total points efficiency. **Jose Caballero** (54.79) remains active despite a bottom-of-the-order assignment because his unique combination of speed and park factors outweighs the marginal gains of the bench. **Vinnie Pasquantino** was the closest to cracking the starting nine (51.00), but his heavy platoon split against the southpaw Jump forced his relocation to the bench in favor of the higher-projected **Austin Riley** and **Josh Naylor**. While **Cole Young** remains a viable depth piece, his lower base projection against Gasser rendered him insufficient to displace our current starters. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood** and **Tyler Soderstrom**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, as we look to maximize our remaining games played against the league leaders.",
